  "fullText": "Resources\nBLOG\nABOUT\nCASE STUDIESCAREERS\n844-496-5673\nGROW MY GYM\n#GYMOWNERSRULE\nTHE MISSION\n\nTo help gym owners around the world reach more people, transform more lives, and build the business of their dreams.\n‍\nWe know we will be successful when every gym owner can provide abundantly for their family, have time to enjoy their lives, and consistently provide life-changing service to their clients. At the end of the day, it’s not about us. It's about you.\n\nJoin The Mission\nABOUT US\nTHE 6 CORE TENETS\nTHAT FUEL GYM LORDS\nDO THE BORING WORK\n\nGoing the extra mile is more than just doing busy work. It’s doing what our competition won’t do. Giving customer service that is noteworthy. Doing it right no matter the short term cost. It’s going that extra mile that truly sets us apart.\n\n\nSPEED IS KING\n\nSpeed is the number one currency in business relationships. SPEED is more important than perfection. Too many opportunities are missed because a project took too long. A good plan executed now is better than a perfect plan executed next week. Because what works now might not work next week.\n\n\nBE YOUR OWN BOSS\n\nHold YOURSELF to a higher standard than anyone else would ask of you. Manage your own time and resources and OWN your decisions and outcomes as if this were your company. Make decisions that can make the company better. When we all be our own boss, the company thrives.\n\n\nGROW OR DIE\n\nLearn fast, fail fast, try again. That’s how you grow. You are either growing (making progress) or dying (stagnation/decline of progress) there is no in between. As a company, we are always ahead of the market even if only by a few steps. Without that edge, we die.\n\n\nHAVE HUMILITY\n\nHumility is keeping the business’ needs above your own. Humble people admit their deficits and grow. When making a decision, they are concerned with WHAT is right, not WHO is right. To have a business that continues to thrive, hire and promote for humility and fire for ego and pride.\n\n\nDON'T SUGAR COAT IT\n\nTruth is best left untampered with. Someone else’s reaction to the truth is not your responsibility. When you sugar coat it, you serve no one by not giving people the opportunity to improve. Without improvement, we become a stagnant fish stuck going against the stream. The amount you grow is directly correlated with the amount of uncomfortable conversations you are willing to have, not by sugar coating it.\n\n\nMEET THE TEAM\nCOACHES\n\nThe Gym Launch coaching team brings decades of combined operational experience from gym ownership, multi-location leadership, and successful exits. Collectively, they've managed over $740M in annual revenue, built gyms from garages to 500+ members, achieved multiple six and seven-figure exits, and transformed struggling facilities from losses to six-figure monthly revenue.\n\nThese are real current and former Gym Owners who've lived every stage of the journey— from living the struggle to scaling past the ceiling that stops most owners. What unites this team is a shared philosophy: boring work over shortcuts, execution over talk, and systems over chaos. They coach from experience, not textbooks, having applied Gym Launch systems to their own businesses and witnessed the transformation firsthand.\n\nRYAN CARSON\nDIRECTOR OF COACHING\nROD BUSBY\nCOACH\nR.E. LEWIS\nCOACH\nMATT MORSE\nCOACH\nBLAKE HILL\nCOACH\nEXECUTIVE\nBRIAN ANDERSON\nCEO\nMIKE FERREIRA\nPRESIDENT\nREADY TO GROW?\nBOOK A CALL WITH OUR TEAM\nBook A Call\nTerms and Conditions\nAll rights reserved.\n(844) 496-5673\nQUICK LINKS\nAbout Us\nPartner With Gym Launch\nCase Studies\nJoin Mission\nBlog\nCookie Policy\nPrivacy Policy\nRESOURCES\n7 Money Models\nStart a Gym Series\nSecrets Book\nSOCIAL\nFacebook\nInstagram\nTik Tok\nYoutube\nTwitter\nNotice at collection\nYour Privacy Choices\nYour consent preferences for tracking technologies"
